# --- Never commit cartridge images or anything derived from them -------------
# This is the project's most important rule. The client ships no cartridge data;
# every player supplies their own file and extraction happens locally.
*.gba
*.gbc
*.gb
*.nds
*.sav
*.srm

# Extractor output — derived from a player's own cartridge, never redistributable.
out/
extracted/
assets/extracted/

# The two files the exporter writes, wherever anybody happens to run it from. These
# are cartridge-derived and the rule at the top of this file covers them; they were
# only ever kept out of the repository by nobody having put one in the root, which is
# not the same as a rule. One got committed the moment somebody did.
world.dat
rules.dat
*/world.dat
*/rules.dat
**/world.dat
**/rules.dat

# The account database, which is nobody else's business either.
players.db

# --- .NET --------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
artifacts/
TestResults/

# --- Editors -----------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Client configuration — points at the player's own cartridge.
client.json

# Server database — accounts and saves. Contains password hashes; never committed.
# The -wal and -shm files are SQLite's write-ahead log and shared memory.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.godot/

# Delivery bundles. This project is handed over as git bundles rather than pushed, so
# one of these lands in a working copy fairly often — including dropped straight into
# the folder by tooling that cannot then remove it. Ignored rather than tidied up by
# hand each time.
*.bundle

# The working copy's own archive of superseded material.
OLD UPDATES DONT USE/
